## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a scalable, compliant multi-tenant data path with both real-time and batch ingestion, telemetry, and controlled configuration across Azure services.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation with per-tenant partitioning and RBAC
- Real-time (Event Hubs) + batch (Data Factory) pipelines
- Durable Functions orchestration for cross-service workflow
- OpenTelemetry across Functions, Event Hubs, and Data Factory; export to Application Insights
- Secrets and config management via Key Vault and App Configuration
- Autoscaling and cost-aware planning; end-to-end testing and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal OpenTelemetry init in an Azure Function
const { NodeSDK } = require('@opentelemetry/sdk-node');
const { OTLPTraceExporter } = require('@opentelemetry/exporter-otlp-http');
const sdk = new NodeSDK({ 
  traceExporter: new OTLPTraceExporter({ url: process.env.OTLP_URL }), 
});
sdk.start();
```

